      "message": "Say what a backup of a forge is, and prove one restores\n\nThree things hold a forge: the database, the repositories, and the key\nthat signs receipts. The operating guide never said so, and the obvious\ncopy of a live database misses what is still in its WAL. scripts/backup.sh\ntakes all three into one bundle through sqlite's backup API, checks the\ncopy's integrity before keeping it, and prunes old bundles; the guide\nsays what it does, why, and how to restore. The first-run walk now ends\nby backing up the forge it just used, restoring the bundle beside it, and\nrunning fsck on the copy, so the claim that a backup restores is one a\nrunner reproduces.\n\nChange-Id: Ibackup0087bundle\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
